I've come to the conclusion that this is a bad idea.  Once you've done
the early protection thing, get the hell out of the mines.  Don't go on 
a killing spree and level up rapidly just because you've got protection.

I'll bet your gnome with the fire horn got it from a shop.

I take great pains to police the shops and the levels.  Carve an
Elbereth square and/or put the shop inventory in a chest, to keep it out
of creatures' hands.  And get out of town as soon as you have protection 
and have a fair idea of what's in the stores (e.g., obvious stuff like a
magic lamp or BOH, don't worry about scrolls and potions too much yet,
bring what you can).  And when you're out of the mines, return to the
same sort of careful play you'd have at turn one.  Don't let early
protection make you overconfident.


